        "keyideas": "Slavery — and specifically whether it could expand into new territories — was the central cause of the sectional crisis. Each compromise or ruling meant to settle the question instead sharpened it: the Fugitive Slave Act angered the North, the Kansas–Nebraska Act reopened the territories, Dred Scott denied any federal limit on slavery, and Lincoln's election (on a platform opposing slavery's expansion) triggered secession and war.",
